r b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loxosceles</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your response seemed to consist of rejecting those facts because they didn't fit your completely unsupportable bullshit complaints and fearmongering.</div> </div> </div> </div> Where are your facts? Oh wait! I'm supposed to simply take you at your word? That so cute! How about biased institutions whose sole interest is to promote nuclear power? That's a winner! At least the links I gave you to y'know...<b>facts</b> were objective. The only thing you can give out is, what did you refer to it? <b>bullshit</b>? Seems appropriate enough. If you can't show your homework, then what you have is an opinion. And a rather biased one makes it nothing less than a belief. Not going to change any minds here apparently. So cheers until the next nuclear screw-up... Hmm...for the current topic; <a href=\"http://www.nytimes.com/2014/02/12/world/asia/nuclear-issue-in-limbo-as-indecision-grips-japan.html?_r=0\" target=\"_blank\">Several industrialized countries</a><i> have turned their backs on nuclear power as a result of the Fukushima nuclear disaster, including one that has already begun permanently shutting functioning plants. That country is not Japan. \u201cGermany chose to get rid of nuclear power because of Fukushima, while the United States is still in favor, but what about Japan, where the accident took place?\u201d said Jun Tateno, who has written several books on nuclear power. \u201cWe still have not had a proper public debate about the most fundamental question: Do we want nuclear power\u2019s low-cost electricity for growth, or do we want a safer, nuclear-free society?\u201d</i> /","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactio